{
  "dom_id": "step-q69453",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14196443/assets/70fe7561f7019a01ea671190c26e3d73f8918fcd18172d0c3e3a1a9447d7269e.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the vectors $a$ and $b.$ Which of the following diagrams illustrates the vector addition $a+b.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we draw the vector that is equal to $b$ and has its tail placed at the head of $a.$ \n\nNow, according to the triangle law of addition, the resultant \n\n$$\na+b\n$$\n\nis the vector that goes from the tail of $\\text{a}$ to the head of $\\text{b}$, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14196443/assets/bff135b735a0db0cbc36d0c3f5030ca639b977bb384e7478ad4b0770cfbd6d89.png)",
